<title>UK: Daewoo plans British car engine plant - paper.</title>
<headline>Daewoo plans British car engine plant - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Daewoo Motor Co plans to build a 200 million pounds ($324.5 million) engine plant in the British car industry's traditional West Midlands heartland, paving the way for a full car plant in due course, The Sunday Times newspaper said.</p>
<p>The report said Daewoo was completing a feasibility study for a British car plant which would be capable of producing 100,000 vehicles a year for the west European market.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
